@page
@model ObservabilityModel

<section>
    <h1>Observability wiring</h1>
    <p>
        The service receives an <code>ILogger&lt;WorkItemService&gt;</code> plus <code>ILogStore</code>.
        Every CRUD call writes to both the console logger and the in-memory history so this page can replay the timeline.
    </p>
    <pre><code>public WorkItemService(
    IWorkItemRepository repository,
    ILogger&lt;WorkItemService&gt; logger,
    ILogStore logStore)
{
    _repository = repository;
    _logger = logger;
    _logStore = logStore;
}</code></pre>
    <p>
        Handlers stay thin by calling the service, but you now get log entries for each list/create/update/delete call.
        Scroll the table below to watch the latest messages with UTC timestamps.
    </p>
    <table class="log-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th><span class="hint" data-hint="Recorded in UTC when the service emitted the log.">Timestamp</span></th>
                <th><span class="hint" data-hint="The message describes the method and payload context.">Message</span></th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        @foreach (var entry in Model.Entries)
        {
            <tr>
                <td>@entry.Timestamp.ToString("u")</td>
                <td>@entry.Message</td>
            </tr>
        }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>
